  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual message implying personal experience",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'when a cop pulls his gun on you but you're white gotcha', which uses the second-person pronoun 'you' to directly address the viewer, creating an implicit identification with the subject of the scenario. The user is invited to imagine themselves as the 'you' in the situation, experiencing the 'gotcha' moment described. This projection is reinforced by the visual metaphor of the hand gesture, which represents the gun, making the scenario feel immediate and personal to the viewer.",
